      <section id="fullstack" aria-labelledby="fullstack-heading">
        <p class="section-label">E5</p>
        <h2 id="fullstack-heading">Full-Stack Development</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Capability to ship small business systems and analytical product UIs: typed front ends, API routes, relational persistence, auth, and evidence-aware tooling. Full Stack JavaScript certified (The Odin Project).</p>

        <h3>How I build software</h3>
        <ol class="workflow">
          <li>Clarify the business problem, users, and non-goals.</li>
          <li>Map the happy path and the failure cases that matter (conflicts, empty slots, bad input).</li>
          <li>Sketch entities and constraints before UI chrome.</li>
          <li>Choose a stack that fits the problem size — not a larger one for show.</li>
          <li>Structure the repo: pages/UI, API routes, shared lib, database schema.</li>
          <li>Build the core flow end-to-end before secondary pages.</li>
          <li>Validate input at the boundary; keep business rules in one place.</li>
          <li>Persist with database constraints that match the real rule (for example unique booking start times).</li>
          <li>Add auth and admin only where ownership decisions are required.</li>
          <li>Wire side effects deliberately (email, notifications) after the write path is sound.</li>
          <li>Test critical paths and adversarial cases; keep analysis logic separate from UI shells.</li>
          <li>Deploy, set environment config, and verify the live path matches local behaviour.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Architecture pattern</h3>
        <div class="arch" role="img" aria-label="Architecture flow from user interface through frontend, API, database, to results">
          <div class="arch-row">
            <div class="arch-cell"><div class="label">Layer</div><div class="val">UI</div></div>
            <div class="arch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
            <div class="arch-cell"><div class="label">Layer</div><div class="val">Frontend</div></div>
            <div class="arch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
            <div class="arch-cell"><div class="label">Layer</div><div class="val">API</div></div>
            <div class="arch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
            <div class="arch-cell"><div class="label">Layer</div><div class="val">Database</div></div>
            <div class="arch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
            <div class="arch-cell"><div class="label">Layer</div><div class="val">Results</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="arch-caption">Example (Bibiunique): Book page → Next.js/React → /api/availability &amp; /api/bookings → PostgreSQL + Prisma → confirmation email + admin review</div>
        </div>

        <h3>What I can build</h3>
        <div class="build-grid">
          <div class="build-cell">
            <h3>Booking systems</h3>
            <p>Service catalogues, availability APIs, conflict-safe bookings, admin approval.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="build-cell">
            <h3>Executive BI product UIs</h3>
            <p>Multi-view dashboards with alerts, reconciliation language, and charted KPIs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="build-cell">
            <h3>Evidence-based tools</h3>
            <p>Document parsing, structured matching, CLI + web UI over a tested engine.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="build-cell">
            <h3>Analytics pipelines</h3>
            <p>Cleaning, SQL/Python EDA, KPI definition, and decision-ready reporting.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="build-cell">
            <h3>Lightweight web utilities</h3>
            <p>Semantic HTML/CSS/JS tools for simple operational lookups and portals.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="build-cell">
            <h3>API-backed scripts</h3>
            <p>External REST consumption with structured export for further analysis.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3>Featured applications</h3>

        <article class="project featured">
          <figure class="project-media">
       